<title>SWEDEN: Incentive posts higher 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Incentive posts higher 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish holding company Incentive AB's profits for the year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			     (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Profit after financial items</p>
<p>   excluding associated companies   3,442  vs  2,624</p>
<p>Profit after financial items,</p>
<p>  including associated companies    5,228  vs  4,653</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)			     42.18  vs  35.55</p>
<p> Dividend				   10.00  vs   9.00</p>
<p> Sales				     20,220  vs 24,324</p>
<p> Gambro unit sales		     10,964  vs 10,157</p>
<p> Gambro operating profit		1,490  vs  1,501</p>
<p> Operating costs			 14,786  vs 19,945</p>
<p> Depreciation immaterial assets	 640  vs    250</p>
<p> Depreciation other			 744  vs    890</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	4,050  vs  3,239</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE 608  vs    615 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					2,241  vs  1,674</p>
<p> Minorities				   103  vs    548</p>
<p> Net profit				 2,884  vs  2,431</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Swedish investment company is Incentive AB. Analysts expected it to post profit of 5.35 billion crowns after financial items and including associate interests, a Reuter poll showed.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
